! Task
! 
! The Goal of the Game:
! 
! The objective of the Hungarian Rings puzzle is to sort the colored balls
! (elements) so that each ring contains continuous blocks of identical
! colors, matching the puzzle's initial solved state.
! 
! How the Game Works:
! 
! • The Board Layout: The game consists of two intersecting rings (Ring 1
! and Ring 2), each holding 12 colored balls. Because the rings overlap,
! they share two specific intersection points (positions 4 and 10 in the
! code).
! 
! • The Core Mechanism: When you rotate a ring, all the balls within that
! ring shift sequentially clockwise. When a ring is rotated, the balls
! currently sitting in the intersection points are carried over into the
! other ring. This allows you to transfer colored balls from one loop to
! the other.
! 
! • Gameplay Loop:
! 
!    1. The player clicks "Shuffle" to randomly rotate the rings 20 times and scramble the colors.
!    2. The player must then use the "Rotate Ring 1" and "Rotate Ring 2" buttons strategically.
!    3. By carefully utilizing the two intersection points, the player must sort the mixed-up colors back into their original grouped patterns.


